1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,351
Aarav puts two dots on a map.

2
00:00:02,351 --> 00:00:03,507
One is his home.

3
00:00:03,507 --> 00:00:05,121
The other is his college.

4
00:00:05,521 --> 00:00:07,384
A straight road joins them.

5
00:00:07,384 --> 00:00:12,304
He wants one rule that says, for any
spot on the map: is it on this road,

6
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:13,204
or not?

7
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,658
He has only the two dots to go on.

8
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:19,712
Can two dots really describe
a road that goes on forever?

9
00:00:20,212 --> 00:00:21,112
Yes.

10
00:00:20,653 --> 00:00:23,772
Two dots, or even one dot
and a slope, are enough.

11
00:00:23,772 --> 00:00:24,843
Let us see how.

12
00:00:25,494 --> 00:00:28,092
First, what is the equation of a line?

13
00:00:28,092 --> 00:00:30,366
It is a rule that links x and y.

14
00:00:30,766 --> 00:00:33,069
Every point on the line obeys the rule.

15
00:00:33,069 --> 00:00:35,149
Every point off the line breaks it.

16
00:00:35,149 --> 00:00:36,919
Like a password for the line.

17
00:00:37,519 --> 00:00:40,977
Start with one fixed
point, P zero, at one, two.

18
00:00:40,977 --> 00:00:42,740
And a slope of one half.

19
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:48,106
Now let a point P, with coordinates
x and y, slide along the line.

20
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:51,088
Watch the slope from P zero to P.

21
00:00:51,088 --> 00:00:52,314
Rise over run.

22
00:00:52,314 --> 00:00:53,648
Zero point five.

23
00:00:53,648 --> 00:00:55,373
Still zero point five.

24
00:00:55,373 --> 00:00:56,762
It never changes.

25
00:00:57,162 --> 00:00:58,865
Now push P off the line.

26
00:00:58,865 --> 00:01:00,606
The slope changes at once.

27
00:01:00,606 --> 00:01:01,810
Zero point eight.

28
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:02,827
Not one half.

29
00:01:03,227 --> 00:01:07,922
So a point is on the line exactly when
the slope from P zero to it equals

30
00:01:07,922 --> 00:01:08,822
m.

31
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:09,663
That is our rule.

32
00:01:10,313 --> 00:01:13,369
Let us write that rule
down, in small steps.

33
00:01:13,769 --> 00:01:14,718
Step one.

34
00:01:14,718 --> 00:01:20,127
The slope from P zero to P is y
minus y zero, over x minus x zero.

35
00:01:20,877 --> 00:01:21,777
Step two.

36
00:01:21,672 --> 00:01:25,081
For P to be on the line,
this slope must equal m.

37
00:01:25,831 --> 00:01:26,833
Step three.

38
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:29,697
Multiply both sides by x minus x zero.

39
00:01:30,447 --> 00:01:31,412
Step four.

40
00:01:31,412 --> 00:01:35,082
y minus y zero equals m
times, x minus x zero.

41
00:01:35,082 --> 00:01:37,367
This is the point slope form.

42
00:01:38,117 --> 00:01:42,768
For our line, y minus two equals
one half times, x minus one.

43
00:01:43,418 --> 00:01:46,511
Now, what if we know two
points, and no slope?

44
00:01:46,911 --> 00:01:47,811
Step one.

45
00:01:47,748 --> 00:01:50,216
Find the slope from the two points.

46
00:01:50,216 --> 00:01:53,388
y two minus y one, over x two minus x one.

47
00:01:54,138 --> 00:01:55,038
Step two.

48
00:01:54,865 --> 00:01:58,520
Put that slope into the point
slope form, at the first point.

49
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:01,005
This is the two point form.

50
00:02:01,005 --> 00:02:03,192
It needs nothing but the two points.

51
00:02:03,842 --> 00:02:04,829
Side by side.

52
00:02:04,829 --> 00:02:07,698
Point slope form needs
one point and the slope.

53
00:02:08,098 --> 00:02:10,193
Two point form needs two points.

54
00:02:10,193 --> 00:02:13,566
It finds the slope for you,
then does the same job.

55
00:02:14,166 --> 00:02:15,066
Your turn.

56
00:02:15,029 --> 00:02:18,646
A line passes through two,
three with slope minus one.

57
00:02:18,646 --> 00:02:20,173
Which form fits best?

58
00:02:20,173 --> 00:02:21,441
Pause and decide.

59
00:02:24,641 --> 00:02:25,673
Point slope!

60
00:02:25,673 --> 00:02:27,428
One point and a slope.

61
00:02:27,428 --> 00:02:31,097
y minus three equals minus
one times, x minus two.

62
00:02:31,747 --> 00:02:32,950
Remember this.

63
00:02:32,950 --> 00:02:35,625
One point and a slope fix a line.

64
00:02:35,625 --> 00:02:39,345
y minus y zero equals m
times, x minus x zero.

65
00:02:40,045 --> 00:02:42,308
One kind of line breaks this form.

66
00:02:42,308 --> 00:02:44,274
A vertical line has no slope.

67
00:02:44,674 --> 00:02:49,806
Every point on it has the same x, so
its rule is just x equals a number.

68
00:02:49,806 --> 00:02:52,945
A horizontal line has
rule y equals a number.

69
00:02:53,545 --> 00:02:54,445
Quick one.

70
00:02:54,376 --> 00:02:57,518
A line passes through
four, one and four, six.

71
00:02:57,518 --> 00:02:58,989
What is its equation?

72
00:02:58,989 --> 00:03:00,164
Pause and think.

73
00:03:03,364 --> 00:03:04,523
x equals four!

74
00:03:04,523 --> 00:03:08,595
Both points have x equal to
four, so the line is vertical.

75
00:03:08,595 --> 00:03:11,282
The slope formula would divide by zero.

76
00:03:11,932 --> 00:03:13,622
Now, one worked example.

77
00:03:13,972 --> 00:03:18,189
Find the equation of the line through
one, minus one, and three, five.

78
00:03:18,689 --> 00:03:19,589
Step one.

79
00:03:19,518 --> 00:03:23,371
The slope is five minus minus
one, over three minus one.

80
00:03:23,371 --> 00:03:24,463
Six over two.

81
00:03:24,463 --> 00:03:25,363
Three.

82
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:26,730
Step two.

83
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:29,063
Use the point one, minus one.

84
00:03:29,063 --> 00:03:32,807
y minus minus one equals
three times, x minus one.

85
00:03:33,557 --> 00:03:34,495
Step three.

86
00:03:34,495 --> 00:03:37,391
So y plus one equals three x minus three.

87
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:39,971
That is y equals three x minus four.

88
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:41,621
Step four.

89
00:03:41,566 --> 00:03:43,254
Check with three, five.

90
00:03:43,254 --> 00:03:45,990
Three times three, minus four, is five.

91
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:46,890
It works.

92
00:03:47,436 --> 00:03:48,897
Now, the exam trap.

93
00:03:49,247 --> 00:03:52,579
A line through minus two,
five with slope four.

94
00:03:52,579 --> 00:03:56,970
Many students write y minus five
equals four times, x minus two.

95
00:03:57,370 --> 00:03:59,428
But x zero is minus two.

96
00:03:59,428 --> 00:04:02,077
x minus minus two is x plus two.

97
00:04:02,077 --> 00:04:06,829
The right form is y minus five
equals four times, x plus two.

98
00:04:07,479 --> 00:04:08,845
Where is this asked?

99
00:04:08,845 --> 00:04:13,180
In JEE Main, for example in January
twenty nineteen: find a line's equation

100
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:15,682
from the points where it meets the axes.

101
00:04:16,282 --> 00:04:17,487
Exam level now.

102
00:04:17,487 --> 00:04:22,396
The line through A and B meets the y
axis at zero, k, and passes through

103
00:04:22,396 --> 00:04:23,437
a, fifteen.

104
00:04:23,437 --> 00:04:24,652
Find k plus a.

105
00:04:24,652 --> 00:04:25,907
Pause and solve.

106
00:04:31,307 --> 00:04:32,860
The answer is B.

107
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,760
Seven.

108
00:04:34,094 --> 00:04:37,788
The slope is eleven minus
three, over six minus two.

109
00:04:37,788 --> 00:04:39,069
Eight over four.

110
00:04:39,069 --> 00:04:39,969
Two.

111
00:04:40,099 --> 00:04:41,563
Point slope at A.

112
00:04:41,563 --> 00:04:44,937
y minus three equals
two times, x minus two.

113
00:04:44,937 --> 00:04:47,197
So y equals two x minus one.

114
00:04:47,697 --> 00:04:52,042
At x equals zero, y is minus
one, so k is minus one.

115
00:04:52,042 --> 00:04:55,728
Fifteen equals two a
minus one, so a is eight.

116
00:04:55,728 --> 00:04:57,373
k plus a is seven.

117
00:04:57,973 --> 00:04:59,513
Here is your recap.

118
00:04:59,513 --> 00:05:01,096
Screenshot this card.

119
00:05:04,296 --> 00:05:06,482
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

120
00:05:06,882 --> 00:05:07,782
One.

121
00:05:07,298 --> 00:05:09,943
Write the line through
the origin with slope two.

122
00:05:10,843 --> 00:05:11,743
Two.

123
00:05:11,332 --> 00:05:15,074
Which line can the point slope
form not describe, and why?

124
00:05:15,974 --> 00:05:16,874
Three.

125
00:05:16,469 --> 00:05:19,979
What is the slope of the line
through one, one and two, three?

126
00:05:21,079 --> 00:05:24,655
Next time: where does the road
cross the two main streets?

127
00:05:24,655 --> 00:05:26,804
Slope intercept and intercept forms.
